"What happens to a request when a call to a store other than `local` fails, takes longer than `quarkus.http.rate-limit.store-timeout`, or is refused because the circuit breaker of the store is open or 256 calls are already in flight: `local` decides it with an in-memory bucket of this replica, `open` lets it through, `closed` answers `503 Service Unavailable` with a `Retry-After` between one and two circuit breaker delays, chosen at random. Applies to the built-in `redis` store, unless `quarkus.http.rate-limit.redis.failure-mode` is set, and to every custom store.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_HTTP_RATE_LIMIT_STORE_FAILURE_MODE+++[]\n"
"--"
